    <string name="help_text"><b>What does the app do?</b>\nA home-screen widget with your next appointments, optionally with contact birthdays and open tasks.\n\n<b>Setup</b>\n1. Allow calendar access.\n2. Choose the calendars to show.\n3. \"Add widget to home screen\" or place it via the launcher widget list.\n\n<b>Settings</b>\nNumber of events and days, location, font, size and colours apply to the widget being edited; the preview shows the result. Tapping an event opens it in the calendar.\n\n<b>Tasks</b>\nOpen tasks are read from the free app Tasks.org, which syncs Google Tasks.\n\n<b>Calendar colors</b>\nGoogle calendars use the Google palette and send the color to Google. Exchange and local calendars keep it on this device only; \"Restore device-only colors\" puts it back after a sync resets it.\n\n<b>Save / load</b>\nThe icons at the top store the display settings in a file and restore them. Calendars and task lists are chosen again on each phone.</string>
